From cf41cd14ca246689230806d9ec97f70138f1af27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cycles Houdini engine authoring <engine@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:13:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 113/113] Update the flags of only the written objects when no
 volume exists

The object flags pass walked every object, recomputed its volume, shadow
catcher, nested dielectric, corner normal and volume intersection bits and
copied the whole flag array on every object or light edit. When the
transforms step of the update wrote only a few objects (the partial object
table, which rewrites their base flags), the last full pass found no
volume object, no flags update was requested (nested dielectrics,
displacement, full rewrite) and no shader changed in this update, the
flags of every other object are those of the previous pass: only the
written objects are updated and their entries copied. A flags pass that
did not complete after an object update leaves a hand-shake flag set, and
the next pass updates every object.

CYCLES_FULL_OBJECT_FLAGS updates every object as before, as a reference.
CYCLES_VERIFY_OBJECT_FLAGS compares a partial result, on the host and on
every device, with updating every object, and reports a difference as an
error.

Rationale: Each single object or light edit on a scene with 380k instances spent 21-33 ms in the object flags pass walking and copying every object.
Contract: Object flags and volume intersection state equal those of updating every object (checked by CYCLES_VERIFY_OBJECT_FLAGS); any volume object, flags request, shader change or full object table write takes the full pass.
Tests: tests/houdini_object_flags_partial_smoke.py
